# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — nothing here may ever be committed.
#
# .env holds the Salesforce Consumer Secret (read access to the PRODUCTION
# org), the Hugging Face token and the SearXNG secret. The backup patterns
# matter as much as .env itself: `cp .env .env.bak-123456` is the natural
# thing to do before an edit, and an unignored copy leaks exactly the same
# credentials under a name nobody thinks to check.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
.session_secret
.runtime/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data and generated artifacts
#
# The DuckDB warehouse and the LanceDB vector store are rebuildable from
# Salesforce; none of it belongs in version control. The old app.sqlite3
# patterns stay: the file is gone (app state moved to PostgreSQL on
# 2026-08-10) but a pre-migration backup is exactly the kind of thing that
# gets left lying in the working tree, and it holds every conversation.
# PostgreSQL itself lives in the `pgdata` Docker volume, not in the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
# Anchored: unanchored `reports/` matches a directory of that name at ANY
# depth, which silently hid the frontend's app/api/reports route handler
# from git. REPORTS_DIR is a root-level path (or a Docker volume), so the
# leading slash is what this rule always meant.
/reports/
# Runtime upload workspaces only. The bare pattern `uploads/` also swallowed
# frontend/app/api/uploads/ -- SOURCE CODE -- which is how a PR shipped tests
# for Next.js routes that git had silently refused to add, and CI went red on
# a module that existed on the author's disk. Anchor runtime dirs explicitly;
# never ignore a bare directory name that could be a route segment.
/uploads/
/orchestrator/uploads/
/.runtime/uploads/
!frontend/app/api/uploads/
/workspace/
/orchestrator/workspace/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.parquet
lancedb/
sf_dictionary.json
# Quarantine file written by scripts/migrate_sqlite_to_postgres.py — it can
# contain message bodies.
orphaned-rows.json

# Model weights and caches (see VLLM_MODELS_DIR — tens of GB)
models/
*.safetensors
*.gguf
hf-cache/
.techsara/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backups left behind by edits — noise at best, secrets at worst
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / Next.js
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Raw ChatGPT export
#
# chatgptdata/ is every conversation ever had, plus ~3.6k file attachments, and
# it is dense with third-party PII: 68 % of conversations contain someone's
# email address (548 distinct), 67 % a phone number. It must never reach a
# remote. Kept on disk deliberately — it can be re-parsed if ever needed.
#
# See docs/finetune-postmortem/ for why a fine-tune on this corpus was aborted.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
chatgptdata/

# Knowledge-store backups (scripts/backup-knowledge.sh) — never committed
backups/
